From 24841e2bec91c702b3eae32c27fb189f74947cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:37:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 147/149] trans: `--crate-type staticlib` builds a C-consumable
 archive

A `staticlib` crate (new `AST::Crate::Type::StaticLib`, from `--crate-type
staticlib` or `#![crate_type = "staticlib"]`) is a whole program minus
`main`, meant for a non-Rust linker: gccrs links two of them
(libformat_parser, ffi-polonius) into crab1 with g++.  Until now the type
was rejected, and minicargo built such crates as rlibs.

The new `CodegenOutput::StaticArchive` enumerates like an rlib (public
items) plus the `#[no_mangle]`/`#[export_name]` functions an executable
would root, loads the allocator and panic runtime like an executable, and
produces `lib<name>.a` = this crate's object + a glue object + every
dependency's `.rlib.o` (the list the executable link already computes,
including the panic-crate selection).  The glue (allocator shims,
`__rust_alloc_error_handler`, `panic_impl`, the `mrustc_panic_*` TLS) goes
in its own member on purpose: when two mrustc archives are linked into one
program both crate objects are pulled in, but an archive member is only
loaded for a still-undefined symbol, so only one copy of the glue is.

The archiver is `AR_<triple>`, `AR`, `<triple>-ar`, then `ar`; the archive
is removed first so `ar r` can't keep stale members.  Native libraries and
dylib crates the consumer has to add are written to `lib<name>.a.libs` as
a shell-ready fragment and printed as a note (what `rustc --print
native-static-libs` gives).  Deferred codegen writes the compile, glue
compile and `ar` as one `&&` line, since the runner executes one line.
MSVC output is a TODO.

The rlib path (`CodegenOutput::StaticLibrary`, still the empty `.rlib`
plus `.rlib.o`) and the executable path are unchanged: the emitted command
and C for an executable are byte-identical to before.

